# Directed programs for the scripted debugger (--dbg-mode) with action-0 execute triggers
# (--dbg-features bit 256, which run_lockstep.sh sets for the programs of this list). An action-0 trigger is a
# breakpoint exception whose handler skips the instruction, which the random programs cannot take (a skipped
# set-up instruction or loop decrement ruins them), so the corpus here is straight-line code that is safe to
# skip, see dbg_exc.s. Not part of --corpus all: it needs --dbg-mode 1 (without the script it is only a
# program that runs its body once and spins). MAX_RETIRE-terminated, like irq.list and smc.list.
#
# target | max_retire (hex file is verification/lockstep/<target>.hex, built with riscv64-unknown-elf-as/ld/objcopy
# against gen/link.ld, see the program's own header)
dbg_exc|6000
